WEBVTT

00:08:29.588 --> 00:08:31.465
So with these larger telescopes,

00:08:31.465 --> 00:08:33.342
we can address these science questions,

00:08:33.342 --> 00:08:35.052
like searching for exoplanets,

00:08:35.052 --> 00:08:36.720
planets around other stars

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.639
and understanding the formation of stars

00:08:38.639 --> 00:08:40.015
and planetary systems ...

00:08:40.015 --> 00:08:41.934
and looking back to the cosmic dawn --

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:43.727
the literal beginning of time --

00:08:43.727 --> 00:08:47.439
and fundamentally understanding
our own place in the universe.

00:08:48.857 --> 00:08:50.985
But it's not just the size
of the telescopes.

00:08:50.985 --> 00:08:52.570
We can also reduce the cost.

00:08:52.945 --> 00:08:54.697
So the James Webb Space Telescope --

00:08:54.697 --> 00:08:55.781
JWST --

00:08:55.781 --> 00:08:56.907
fantastic instrument,

00:08:56.907 --> 00:08:57.908
amazing.

00:08:58.075 --> 00:08:59.785
The telescope is relatively large,

00:08:59.785 --> 00:09:02.788
so it didn't fit on any existing
launch vehicles.